.TH BATTERY-NOTIFY 1 "2026-09-29" "simple-battery-notify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
battery-notify \- customizable battery notifications from UPower
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B battery-notify show
.br
.B battery-notify status
.br
.B battery-notify daemon
.br
.B battery-notify
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B battery-notify
shows desktop notifications about the battery: when the charger is connected
or disconnected, when the battery reaches the levels you choose, when it is
full, and on demand.
It reads the battery from UPower, over D-Bus.
.PP
It is meant to be scripted: output on stdout is data only, messages go to
stderr, and every outcome has its own exit status.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Notify the current battery state now, using the
.BR "[show discharging]" ,
.B "[show charging]"
or
.B "[show full]"
section. Meant for a keybinding.
.TP
.B status
Print the battery state; see
.BR "STATUS OUTPUT" .
.TP
.B daemon
Watch UPower and notify battery events until stopped. Run by the systemd user
service; see
.BR SERVICE .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH STATUS OUTPUT
.B status
prints four
.IB key = value
lines:
.TP
.B state
.BR charging ,
.BR discharging ,
.BR full ,
.BR empty ,
.B pending-charge
(on AC but not charging, e.g. held at a charge limit),
.B pending-discharge
or
.BR unknown .
.TP
.B percentage
The battery level, rounded down.
.TP
.BR time_to_empty ", " time_to_full
Seconds, as estimated by UPower; 0 when not applicable or not known yet.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
state=discharging
percentage=58
time_to_empty=12960
time_to_full=0
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/battery-notify/config ,
or
.I ~/.config/battery-notify/config
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or not an absolute path.
Without it, built-in defaults apply; they are installed as
.I /usr/share/doc/simple-battery-notify/config.example
to start from.
The file replaces the defaults entirely.
After editing it, restart the service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user restart battery-notify.service
.fi
.RE
.PP
The file is read, never executed.
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
Each section names an event and sets its notification:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[discharging 15]
urgency = critical
title = Battery low
message = Connect the charger: {level}% left
.fi
.RE
.SS Events
.TP
.BI "[discharging " N ]
On battery, the level drops to
.IR N %
or below (1 to 100).
.TP
.BI "[charging " N ]
On AC, the level rises to
.IR N %
or above.
.TP
.B [full]
UPower reports the battery fully charged.
.TP
.BR [plugged] ", " [unplugged]
The charger is connected or disconnected.
.TP
.BR "[show discharging]" ", " "[show charging]" ", " "[show full]"
.B battery-notify show
in that state.
.PP
Levels have a direction: discharging levels never fire while on AC, and
charging levels never fire on battery.
If the level jumps over several levels at once (for example after a suspend),
only the most severe fires: the lowest discharging level, or the highest
charging level.
When the daemon starts on battery at or below a
.B critical
discharging level, the nearest one fires once.
An event without a section is silent.
.SS Keys
.TP
.B title
The notification's title. Required.
.TP
.B message
Its body. Empty by default.
.TP
.B urgency
.BR low ,
.B normal
(default) or
.BR critical .
.TP
.B timeout
How long it stays on screen, in milliseconds (0 to 9999999).
Default 2000, or 0 (until dismissed) for critical notifications.
.SS Placeholders
In
.B title
and
.BR message :
.TP
.B {level}
The battery percentage.
.TP
.B {time}
The time left, as 3h 36m: to empty on battery, to full while charging, or
.B estimating...
while UPower has no estimate yet.
.PP
Any other
.BI { word }
is a mistake.
.SS Mistakes
Every command checks the file first and stops at the first mistake, printing
.IB file : line :
and the problem, with exit status 3.
The daemon also sends a critical notification with the same text, since its
stderr goes to the journal.
.SH SERVICE
The systemd user service runs
.B battery-notify daemon
with your desktop session (it is part of
.BR graphical-session.target ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now battery-notify.service
.fi
.RE
.PP
If UPower goes away, the daemon exits and systemd restarts it after 5 seconds.
After a config mistake, or on a machine without a battery, it stays stopped.
If your session does not activate
.BR graphical-session.target ,
start the daemon another way, for example from your compositor's autostart.
.SH SUSPENDING AT A CRITICAL LEVEL
.B battery-notify
only notifies; it runs no commands.
To suspend, hibernate or power off when the battery is nearly empty, use
UPower's own action, which works even if your session has frozen:
.B PercentageAction
and
.B CriticalPowerAction
in
.IR /etc/UPower/UPower.conf .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Configuration mistake.
.TP
.B 4
System error: UPower unreachable, the connection to it lost, or an unexpected
answer.
.TP
.B 5
No battery.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the battery from a keybinding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
battery-notify show
.fi
.RE
.PP
The percentage, in a script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
battery-notify status | sed \-n 's/^percentage=//p'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR upower (1),
.BR UPower.conf (5),
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Davi-S/simple-battery-notify/issues
